@startuml StartupDispatch
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: how proveo consumes sbx's startup dispatcher on Docker's documented terms — what blocks, what runs beside the agent, and the probe that pins the contract
' covers: internal/sbx/kit.go
' covers: internal/sbx/sbx_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/startup_commands_test.go
' covers: packages/lib/proveo-seed
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: internal/contract/seed_phase_test.go
' covers: e2e/startup_dispatch_test.go
' covers: scripts/proveo-jitter-probe.py
' covers: e2e/seed_ready_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/agents.go
' covers: internal/imagetest/cecli_test.go
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── AUTHORITATIVE SOURCE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   kits : https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/kits/  (read 2026-10-13)
' What Docker documents about sbx governs how proveo consumes it. A measurement
' that disagrees is a probe result to report upstream, never a behaviour to
' build on.
'
' ── THE DOCUMENTED RULE, QUOTED ─────────────────────────────────────────────
'   background (default false): "Block later startup commands until this
'   command finishes. Set to true to let later commands run without waiting."
'
'   "They also don't gate the agent's entrypoint: the agent launches once
'   startup commands have been dispatched, regardless of background. A value
'   of false waits within the startup dispatcher before it runs the next
'   command; it doesn't delay the agent entrypoint. Use startup commands for
'   work that can run alongside the agent. Use setup.files for any value that
'   needs to land on disk before the agent runs."
'
'   "Startup commands must be idempotent. They run on every sandbox start and
'   replay on container restarts."
'
' ── WHAT WAS MEASURED, 2026-10-13, proveo-claudecode-f8781ef6 ───────────────
' Read from inside the VM: /proc/stat btime, process start times, file ctimes,
' /var/log/sbx-kit-startup.log.
'   16:43:06        VM boot (PID 1)
'   16:43:09        dispatcher starts; sbx's own claude-kit steps take <1s
'   16:43:10–41     .claude config restore: 12,873 files / 966 MB, one cp per
'                   file; 7,093 files / 866 MB were ONE jobs/<id>/tmp tree
'   16:43:42        release marker: subagents, settings, hooks in place
'   16:43:43–44:07  toolchain restore: 1.7 GB / 66,552 entries
'   16:44:09–20     pnpm install into the fresh clone
'   16:44:21–32     the seed-only entrypoint pass re-ran the whole seed
'   16:44:32        agent forked (PPID 0), CDP relay up, dispatcher complete
' Every Kit step was foreground: KitCommand had no background field at all.
' The agent forked when the dispatcher returned, 86s after boot and ~50s after
' the release said it could run. Whatever sbx keyed that fork on, proveo had
' put install work into steps the docs reserve for "alongside the agent" and
' declared none of it background.
'
' ── THE SEED IS THREE STARTUP STEPS, FOR A BUILT-IN sbx AGENT ──────────────
'   1  proveo-seed <target> release       foreground. Checkout, shares,
'                                         instructions, state and config
'                                         restore, hooks, subagents, wiring,
'                                         the chrome bridge, then the
'                                         release marker.
'   2  PROVEO_SEED_PHASE=none entrypoint  foreground, mixins only. The def's
'                                         own wiring; its proveo_seed call
'                                         returns at once, step 1 did it.
'   3  proveo-seed <target> provision     background: true, always LAST.
'                                         Tool restore, then the tool env
'                                         block at once, toolchain, deps,
'                                         LSPs, the second wire pass, then
'                                         seed-done.
' Step 3 is last because background lets LATER steps run beside it: placed
' earlier, the def's wiring would race the installs.
'
' ONLY a target with a built-in sbx agent (claudecode, codex, cursor, opencode)
' splits. Their agent command is the harness binary, so nothing in the agent
' process seeds. cecli and hermes run their def entrypoint AS the agent (an
' own-agent Kit, or ShellLaunch when PROVEO_SBX_AGENT_KIT=0), and that
' entrypoint seeds inline before it execs. A background step 3 there would
' install beside that inline seed — two pnpm installs in one workspace, two
' `mise use -g` into one MISE_DATA_DIR — so those Kits keep one foreground
' `proveo-seed <target> all`, exactly the old shape.
'
' ── STEP 2 FINDS THE DEF'S ENTRYPOINT THE WAY ShellLaunch DOES ─────────────
' Not every image ships /entrypoint.sh. cecli's entrypoint is
' /usr/local/bin/cecli-entrypoint, and the cecli image has no /entrypoint.sh.
' Step 2 named /entrypoint.sh outright, so on cecli `env` exited 127 and sbx
' failed the sandbox start ("kit startup exited with code 127"). That hit
' every mixin-kit cecli run: `--shell` (retired 2026-10-17), and
' PROVEO_SBX_AGENT_KIT=0. It predates
' the split: base e66eb45c (#68) carried the same argv. Found 2026-10-14 by
' TestSeedReleasesEveryHarnessReady/cecli.
' Step 2 now execs <target>-entrypoint when PATH has it, else /entrypoint.sh,
' the order ShellLaunch launches in (defEntrypoint, internal/sbx/agents.go).
' su's PATH keeps /usr/local/bin, so the lookup holds inside the dispatcher.
' An image with neither exits 0: it has no def wiring to run, and a failing
' step ends the start. internal/imagetest/cecli_test.go runs the Kit's own
' argv in the image under su's PATH and requires cecli's "seed-only" line.
'
' The chrome bridge moved BEFORE the release. It needs only node, which the
' image bakes, takes at most 3s, and writes hasCompletedClaudeInChromeOnboarding
' into ~/.claude.json with a plain read-then-write. After the release that write
' would race Claude Code's own writes to the same file, and the onboarding
' dialog it suppresses is one no automation answers
' (_spec/defs/claudecode/chrome-bridge.puml).
'
' The gate the agent waits on stays proveo's own: proveo-await-seed polls the
' release marker for PROVEO_INSTRUCTIONS_WAIT (30s). The docs make that gate
' necessary, since no startup step holds the agent. Step 1 therefore has to
' finish inside 30s of boot, which is why the config restore stopped forking
' per file and skips transient scratch
' (_spec/packages/lib/config-seeding-and-persistence.puml).
'
' KNOWN GAP, older than this split: the marker lands at the end of step 1, so
' step 2's def wiring (opencode's Ollama provider, cursor's useHttp1ForAgent) is
' not behind it. Under the documented model the agent can start before that
' wiring, as it could before; the def wiring has to move into the seed, or the
' marker after step 2, to close it.
'
' The phase is an ARGUMENT to proveo-seed and proveo_seed; PROVEO_SEED_PHASE is
' the env spelling a def entrypoint inherits from step 2. "all" is the default
' and is what docker runs: there is no dispatcher there, the entrypoint seeds
' and then execs.
'
' ── MARKERS, ALL ON /dev/shm (a per-container tmpfs: a restart starts clean) ─
'   proveo-seed-done      the installs are over. A release or all phase clears
'                         it first; provision (or all) writes it last.
'   proveo-seed-refused   a share is missing. Step 3 provisions nothing.
'                         (Until D2, also "OpenCode history is
'                         unprepared"; D2 deleted that gate, 2026-10-17 —
'                         _spec/defs/opencode/engine-local-history.puml.)
'   proveo-seed-halted    the release phase returned non-zero (an OpenCode
'                         default missing, an unknown phase). Step 3 provisions
'                         nothing, as the single seed stopped there before.
'   proveo-provisioning   step 3's pid while it installs. The teardown's
'                         toolchain save skips while that pid lives, so a
'                         one-shot run that ends mid-install never stamps a
'                         half-installed tree as a clean save
'                         (_spec/internal/sbx/state-sync.puml).
'
' ── VERSION SKEW ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A new image under an old Kit sees no phase and runs "all": the old timing.
' An old image under a new Kit ignores the argument and the env. Step 1 runs
' the full seed in the foreground and marks seed-done; step 3's wrapper is
' rendered on the HOST, needs no rebuilt image, and exits when seed-done
' exists. A new image's release phase never writes it, so the check tells the
' two apart. Step 2 on an old image ignores PROVEO_SEED_PHASE=none and seeds
' again — the old behaviour, no worse. [Unverified] An sbx that predates the
' `background` field would refuse the Kit outright if its loader is strict;
' the host sbx at 2026-10-13 renders its own claude kit with a background step.
'
' ── EVERY SEED STEP EXITS 0 (seedNeverAbort, internal/sbx/kit.go) ──────────
' sbx's durable-startup dispatcher runs each startup command under `set -e`
' and `exit $rc`, so one non-zero step tears down a live agent session. A seed
' miss is a warning, never that: the -c wrapper runs proveo-seed, prints a
' non-zero status to stderr, and exits 0. The wrap lives on the host Kit so it
' takes effect without rebuilding the image that ships proveo-seed
' (_spec/internal/sbx/seed-node-version-abort.puml).
'
' ── WHAT THE SPLIT ACCEPTS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Installs now run beside a live agent on every model sbx might follow. The
' agent can call a tool before step 3 restores or installs it; the tool env
' block lands right after the restore, and Claude Code's shells source it per
' command (proveo_install_claude_env_hook), so restored tools appear first and
' installed ones as they finish. The agent's own installs can race step 3's in
' the same workspace. The second wire pass still rewrites LSP wiring after the
' agent started, as the seed-and-launch order already accepted.
'
' ── THE PROBE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' e2e/startup_dispatch_test.go starts STOCK sbx — no proveo image, no proveo
' seed — with a one-step mixin whose step sleeps, in two rows: FOREGROUND (the
' docs' own claim) and BACKGROUND (the one this split relies on). The shell
' agent records its own start. The docs say it starts before the sleep ends;
' each row fails otherwise and prints `sbx version` plus the timestamps, which
' is the upstream report already written. A failing background row means the
' split buys nothing on that sbx; a failing foreground row alone means sbx
' gates on foreground steps, which the split already routes around.
'
' TestSeedReleasesEveryHarnessReady (e2e/seed_ready_test.go) launches every
' sbx harness through its own kit (`proveo run <target>`, host PTY proxy
' included) — since 2026-10-17, when `--shell` was retired; before that every
' harness but opencode ran `proveo run <target> --shell` — so it carries this
' guard instead of a second launch. It waits for the harness's own prompt text
' (readySpec.ready: claudecode "bypass permissions", codex "Ask Codex to do
' anything", opencode "Ask anything", cursor "Cursor Agent"; cecli and hermes
' have none and wait for the release marker and a quiet pane), then asserts the
' prompt came within 20s of the release marker (assertPromptSoonAfterRelease:
' host time of the prompt minus the guest mtime of the marker). [Unverified]
' That subtraction assumes the host and guest clocks agree. It then types into
' the prompt while the background step may still install: echo p90 <= 250ms,
' max <= 1s (PROVEO_TEST_ECHO_P90 / _ECHO_MAX / _READY_AFTER_RELEASE override).
' Early-input jitter, reported 2026-10-13, is the regression it guards.
' [Unverified] opencode's ready-gap row: under the keeper design the host
' re-ran its seed through `sbx exec` after preparing history, not as a Kit
' startup step, so the gap may not have applied the same way; this pass did
' not read the exemption. Under D2 (DONE (wt) 2026-10-17;
' _spec/defs/opencode/engine-local-history.puml) the host does the one-time
' import between `sbx create` and the reattach and re-runs no seed.
' [Inference] The opencode row then follows the Kit startup steps like every
' other harness.

' ── PROBE RESULT, 2026-10-13, sbx v0.46.0 (991967dc) on the operator's Mac ──
'   foreground row  FAIL  step 1791938970→1791939030 (60s); agent 1791939030.
'                         The agent started the second the step ended.
'   background row  PASS  the agent started while the step still slept.
' So v0.46.0 gates the agent's entrypoint on FOREGROUND startup steps, against
' the docs, and does not wait on background ones. That explains the 86s stall
' and confirms the split: only work in background steps escapes the gate.
' The foreground row's output is the upstream report (docker/sbx-releases).
'
' ── A MEASURED DEVIATION SKIPS, AN UNMEASURED ONE FAILS (2026-10-14) ───────
' foregroundGateVersions in e2e/startup_dispatch_test.go lists the sbx
' releases measured to gate on a foreground step: v0.46.0. On a listed release
' the foreground row skips and logs the same report, so `mise run test-e2e`
' stays green on a deviation already measured and reported. On any other
' release a gating foreground step fails the row, so a new sbx is measured
' before it joins the list. The background row has no list: the split relies
' on it, and a gating background step fails on every release.
'
' ── AFTER THE SPLIT, 2026-10-13, same workspace, fresh VM, sbx v0.46.0 ───────
'   +5s   release marker            (was +36s)
'   +8s   agent forked              (was +86s)
'   +67s  seed-done, background provision step finished beside the agent
' No jobs/*/tmp tree reached the VM. The store had no toolchain token yet, so
' this restore copied in full and wrote none; the first teardown save mints it.

title Startup dispatch — what blocks the agent, what runs beside it

node "Kit setup.startup (dispatcher order)" as KIT <<host>> {
  component "1 · ""proveo-seed <target> release""\nforeground, incl. chrome bridge" as REL <<app>>
  component "2 · ""PROVEO_SEED_PHASE=none /entrypoint\.sh""\nforeground, mixins only" as DEF <<app>>
  component "3 · ""proveo-seed <target> provision""\n""background: true""" as PROV <<async>>
}

component """/dev/shm/proveo-instructions-seeded""\nthe release marker" as MARK <<app>>
component """proveo-await-seed""\n≤ PROVEO_INSTRUCTIONS_WAIT (30s)" as GATE <<app>>
component "agent process" as AGENT <<app>>
component """/dev/shm/proveo-seed-done""" as DONE <<app>>
component "agent forked 86s after boot\nwaiting on installs it never needed" as LATE <<error>>

REL ARROW_MAIN MARK : writes
REL ARROW_MAIN DEF
DEF ARROW_MAIN PROV : dispatched, not awaited
GATE ARROW_MAIN MARK : polls
GATE ARROW_MAIN AGENT : exec once marked
PROV ARROW_OPTIONAL DONE : beside the agent
KIT ARROW_ERROR LATE : every step foreground (before)

note right of REL
  **Docker's docs govern.** Startup steps
  never gate the agent; ""background: false""
  only holds the NEXT step. Work the agent
  needs first ends at the release marker.
end note

note right of PROV
  **Installs run beside the agent.** Last in
  the list, so nothing after it races them;
  a refused step 1 leaves it nothing to do.
end note

note bottom of GATE
  **The only gate is proveo's own.** Step 1
  must beat its 30s, so the config restore
  copies in bulk and skips transient scratch.
end note

note bottom of LATE
  **Measured 2026-10-13.** 12,873 config files
  copied one by one, 1.7 GB of toolchains and a
  second full seed, all in foreground steps.
end note
@enduml
